[{"id":4579253437,"node_id":"PRR_kwDONpzSS88AAAABEPHcvQ","user":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]","id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-pull-request-reviewer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copilot-pull-request-reviewer%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR updates `otelc` to resolve hook and file rule locations through the Go module graph (via `go/packages`) rather than assuming rule sources live under `.otelc-build`. This enables loading rules, hook packages, and injected files from third-party instrumentation modules (motivated by #612).\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add `ResolvedPath` to function/file rules and populate it during setup using `go/packages`, so instrument phase can read rule sources directly from resolved filesystem locations.\n- Update dependency syncing to add `replace` directives based on embedded instrumentation module paths, and extend rule schema/docs with an optional `module` field.\n- Add stub packages (and adjust build tags) so instrumentation packages remain importable even when implementation files are `//go:build ignore`.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 21 out of 21 changed files in this pull request and generated 5 comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tool/util/shared.go | Adds constants for package/module roots used across setup/sync logic. |\r\n| tool/internal/setup/testdata/single_func_rule.otelc.runtime.go.golden | Updates generated runtime golden output to use `_getstack*` names. |\r\n| tool/internal/setup/testdata/multiple_rule_sets.otelc.runtime.go.golden | Same golden update; also removes an unused import from the generated output. |\r\n| tool/internal/setup/sync.go | Refactors replace-directive creation and updates version-bump warning behavior. |\r\n| tool/internal/setup/sync_test.go | Aligns tests with new constants and structured warning log output. |\r\n| tool/internal/setup/store.go | Resolves rule import paths to filesystem directories during setup and stores them in matched JSON. |\r\n| tool/internal/setup/store_test.go | Adds tests covering successful and failing rule path resolution. |\r\n| tool/internal/setup/setup.go | Passes context/module directories into the store step and updates the store output description. |\r\n| tool/internal/setup/add.go | Separates func/file rule imports, avoids mutating the global import map, and fixes generated symbol naming. |\r\n| tool/internal/rule/func_rule.go | Introduces `module` YAML field, defaults module path, and adds `resolved_path` JSON field. |\r\n| tool/internal/rule/file_rule.go | Introduces `module` YAML field, defaults module path, and adds `resolved_path` JSON field. |\r\n| tool/internal/instrument/trampoline.go | Switches hook file discovery to use `ResolvedPath`. |\r\n| tool/internal/instrument/instrument_test.go | Ensures tests populate `ResolvedPath` before writing matched JSON. |\r\n| tool/internal/instrument/apply_file.go | Switches file rule application to use `ResolvedPath` (removing local-path guessing). |\r\n| instrumentation/runtime/stub.go | Adds a stub to keep the runtime package importable. |\r\n| instrumentation/runtime/runtime_gls.go | Marks implementation file as `//go:build ignore` for otelc consumption. |\r\n| instrumentation/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace/stub.go | Adds stub to keep the trace package importable. |\r\n| instrumentation/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric/stub.go | Adds stub to keep the metric package importable. |\r\n| instrumentation/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/provider/trace/stub.go | Adds stub to keep the provider/trace package importable. |\r\n| instrumentation/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/hook/otelc.yaml | Adds `module:` to file rules whose `path` is not a module root. |\r\n| docs/rules.md | Documents the optional `module` field for func/file rules. |\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/617#pullrequestreview-4579253437","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/617","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/617#pullrequestreview-4579253437"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/op